            "title": "Incorrect handling of multiple command line arguments with the same name",
            "severity": "high",
            "file": "lib/cli.js",
            "line": 23,
            "explanation": "This change removed the code that handled the case where a command line argument is provided multiple times, which parsed into an array. Previously, the code took the last occurrence by popping the last value from the array. The new code assigns the entire array instead of a single value, which breaks the expected type for the option and may cause downstream errors.",
            "suggestion": "Restore the logic to detect if argv[name] is an array and assign the last element to options[helper.dashToCamel(name)], to preserve previous behavior of overriding multiple arguments with the last occurrence."
